* Step 7: a pre-existing issue with the old and new versions of tsfactor: the 500MB+ sized checkpoint file ec_with_ckpt.ckpt remains in the directory even after the results file has been successfully written (when the program either terminates or goes to the next s-value). This is harmless to the program's operation because a checkpoint file for one particular s-value will be ignored when working on other s-values, but it does take up disk space (as do the .ckpt.1 and .ckpt.2 files, if applicable)
